-- title:
--   APSP in O(n^2.995561) from any counting oracle running in time n^2.9955609
-- statement:
--   Let procedure $p_O$ of a program $P$ solve the counting oracle task `Light.Filter2.oracleTask` with time $T_o$ and a polynomially bounded need (`PolyNeedN`), and suppose that for all real $c,\kappa$, for all large $n$, every $U\le cn^{\kappa}$ and every modulus $p\le$ `PmaxOf n`, $T_o(n,U,s(n),p)\le n^{2.9955609}$ where $s(n)=$ `Light.Filter2.sOf n` $=2^{\lfloor0.0336175k\rfloor}$. Then
--   $$\mathrm{EndStatement.APSP.SolvedInTime}(2.995561).$$
--
--   The filtering host makes $n^{o(1)}$ oracle calls and solves All-Edges Exact Triangle in time $O(n^{2.99556095})$ along $U\le cn^{\kappa+1}$; the chain to the (min,+)-product and APSP adds polylogarithmic factors.
-- source:
--   Developed for the prove2.me APSP exponent campaign (https://prove2.me/campaigns/apsp-exponent) on top of the Lean formalization anthropics/formal-math, folder 3sum-apsp, commit e1a4e65 (https://github.com/anthropics/formal-math/tree/e1a4e6508154ea59f030480661590a9fe3018011/3sum-apsp; Lean v4.33.1, Mathlib v4.33.1). The statement comes from the file 3sum-apsp/ThreeSumApsp/Filter2/Final.lean of the campaign's modified copy of that library, which is not published; the new definitions it uses are in the platform definition bundles APSP2995561_Defs1 and APSP2995561_Defs2 (and APSP2996001_Defs1-2, APSP299791_Defs1-5 of the earlier entries). It follows the technical note "Deterministic APSP via thin products" (revised 7 October 2026) refining J. Alman and V. Vassilevska Williams, "Truly Subquadratic 3SUM and Truly Subcubic APSP via Triangles in Sparse Lopsided Graphs", arXiv:2610.06783v1 (https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.06783v1), Lemma 3.1 and Theorem 1.1.

